Four sets are NOT under this licence. `gold_de_en`, `mahjongg`, `sepia` and
`treecreeper` are adapted from Wikipedia articles and are under the Creative
Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License (CC BY-SA 4.0).
`LICENSE-CC-BY-SA` in this directory names their sources and the changes made,
and each of the four directories carries its own `LICENSE`.

One set under this licence has an outside source. The two source documents of
`voyager` are adapted from NASA's page on the Voyager 2 mission. Source: NASA.
NASA says its content is generally not subject to copyright in the United
States. Factual errors were planted in the two documents on purpose, as a
test, so they must not be read as NASA's account of the mission.
`voyager/reference.md` is the project author's merge of the two and carries
the correct facts. NASA does not endorse this project. The adaptation is
under this licence.

This licence covers the other fifteen sets of `tests/handwritten/` only. See
`NOTICE` at the repository root for what else in this repository carries
it, and `LICENSE` at the repository root for the code, which is under the
Elastic License 2.0 and not this licence.
